<title>POLAND: Polish macroeconomic forecast for Q4 1996.</title>
<headline>Polish macroeconomic forecast for Q4 1996.</headline>
<text>
<p>Following is a macreconomic forecast for the fourth quarter of 1996, submitted October 16, prepared for Reuters by Tadeusz Chroscicki, chief analyst at the Planning Ministry (CUP).</p>
<p>MAIN ECONOMIC INDICATOR FORECAST</p>
<p>			    SEPTEMBER   OCTOBER   NOVEMBER   DECEMBER</p>
<p>CPI (pct change)</p>
<p>  month/month		 1.9(R)	1.4	 1.1	  1.5</p>
<p>  year/year		  19.5(R)     19.0	18.8	 18.7</p>
<p>  Dec 95 = 100	    114.0(R)    115.6     116.9	118.7</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT</p>
<p>  month/month		 5.2(R)	5.0	 -4.0	 -6.0</p>
<p>  year/year		   8.0(R)     11.5	  8.0	  6.0</p>
<p> UNEMPLOYMENT RATE (pct) 13.5	  13.3	 13.4	 13.5</p>
<p>Following figures in billion USD</p>
<p> OFFICIAL RESERVES	 17.6	 17.8	 17.8	 18.0</p>
<p> NET RESERVES		21.6	 21.7	 21.9	 22.0</p>
<p> C/A TRADE BALANCE	 -5.1	 -5.7	 -6.3	 -7.0</p>
<p>  Exports		    17.7	 20.2	 22.7	 24.9</p>
<p>  Imports		    22.8	 25.9	 29.0	 31.9</p>
<p>		    *********************************</p>
<p>NOTES: Official forex reserves are hard currencies held by the central bank while net reserves are the total amount of foreign exchange in the banking system.</p>
<p>Indicators marked (R) are results, rest are forecasts.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780</p>
